    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials could significantly improve responder ingress and egress, particularly given the limited alternatives for rear access. Posting visible address signage near the street frontage and at the driveway entry would support faster navigation to the correct access point. Maintaining adequate clearance along the driveway corridor may assist larger emergency vehicles in maneuvering to the main building and detached structure. Keeping the outdoor storage area organized and set back from primary travel paths could facilitate unobstructed movement and staging during an emergency response."
